<gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" creator="open-pilgrimages" version="1.1"><metadata><name>Camino Primitivo (Original Way)</name><desc>The original Camino — the route walked by King Alfonso II of Asturias from Oviedo to Santiago in 814 CE shortly after the discovery of the apostle&apos;s tomb. The most physically demanding of the major Caminos, crossing the Asturian and Galician mountains via the high Hospitales/Puerto del Palo route (1,146 m), through the walled Roman city of Lugo, before joining the Camino Francés at Melide for the final descent to Santiago. UNESCO inscribed (2015 Northern Spain extension to the 1993 Camino Francés inscription).</desc><copyright author="OpenStreetMap contributors"><license>https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/</license></copyright><link href="https://open.pilgrimag.es/camino-primitivo"><text>Camino Primitivo (Original Way)</text></link></metadata><trk><name>Camino Primitivo (Original Way)</name><trkseg><trkpt lat="43.358604" lon="-5.840681"/><trkpt lat="43.358716" lon="-5.840863"/><trkpt lat="43.358788" lon="-5.841060"/><trkpt lat="43.358831" lon="-5.841253"/><trkpt lat="43.358843" lon="-5.841405"/><trkpt lat="43.358860" lon="-5.841611"/><trkpt lat="43.358864" lon="-5.841666"/><trkpt lat="43.358888" lon="-5.841963"/><trkpt lat="43.358897" lon="-5.842080"/><trkpt lat="43.358930" lon="-5.842492"/><trkpt lat="43.358942" lon="-5.842633"/><trkpt lat="43.359029" lon="-5.842643"/><trkpt lat="43.359114" lon="-5.842689"/><trkpt lat="43.359193" lon="-5.842766"/><trkpt lat="43.359237" lon="-5.842896"/><trkpt lat="43.359237" lon="-5.842939"/><trkpt lat="43.359238" lon="-5.842968"/><trkpt lat="43.359781" lon="-5.843284"/><trkpt lat="43.359908" lon="-5.843352"/><trkpt lat="43.360036" lon="-5.843399"/><trkpt lat="43.360104" lon="-5.843404"/><trkpt lat="43.360320" lon="-5.843452"/><trkpt lat="43.360378" lon="-5.843461"/><trkpt lat="43.360449" lon="-5.843469"/><trkpt lat="43.360645" lon="-5.843488"/><trkpt lat="43.360900" lon